@startuml Kaigara-Architecture
title Kaigara -- Proposed System Architecture\n(Option A baseline, engine boundary designed for Option C -- see ADR 0001)
skinparam wrapWidth 220
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

actor "Benchmark\nEngineer" as engineer

skinparam component {
  BackgroundColor<<implemented>> #d4edda
  BorderColor<<implemented>> #28a745
  BackgroundColor<<planned>> #fff3cd
  BorderColor<<planned>> #cc9a06
  BackgroundColor<<external>> #e2e3e5
  BorderColor<<external>> #6c757d
}
skinparam database {
  BackgroundColor<<planned>> #fff3cd
  BorderColor<<planned>> #cc9a06
}

package "Kaigara -- ships as a Tauri desktop app or a Docker / server image" {

  component "Frontend (React + TypeScript + Vite)\nConnect / Load / Compose / Run / Analyze" as frontend <<implemented>>

  package "Backend (Fastify orchestrator) -- scaffolding only, not implemented" {
    component "Scenario / Connection / Run store" as store <<planned>>
    component "EngineAdapter interface" as adapterIface <<planned>>
    component "k6 adapter\n(compiles a Scenario's method\nLoadTimeline into a k6 script)" as k6adapter <<planned>>
    component "Correctness checker\n(ajv + official JSON Schemas)" as correctness <<planned>>
    component "Generated OpenAPI client" as openapiclient <<planned>>
  }

  database "SQLite\n(scenarios, runs, time series)" as sqlite <<planned>>
}

component "k6\n(external subprocess -- AGPL,\nnever linked in-process)" as k6 <<external>>
component "aas-test-engines\n(official conformance CLI)" as testengines <<external>>
component "LLM backend\n(hosted API or local Ollama)" as llm <<external>>
component "IDTA aas-specs-api\n(official OpenAPI spec)" as idtaspec <<external>>
component "Target AAS server(s)\n(twinsphere / Eclipse BaSyx)\nvia IDTA-01002 REST API" as target <<external>>

engineer --> frontend : browses / composes\nScenarios, watches runs

frontend --> store : HTTP / WebSocket\n(Scenario CRUD, run control,\nlive metrics -- currently mocked\nin-process, see lib/api/)

store --> sqlite : persist
store --> adapterIface : compile & run
k6adapter ..|> adapterIface : implements
correctness --> openapiclient
store ..> correctness : pre/postcondition\ngates

k6adapter --> k6 : spawn subprocess\nwith compiled script
k6 --> target : load generation

openapiclient --> target : preparation +\ncorrectness-check calls
idtaspec ..> openapiclient : generates client\n(build-time, via openapi-to-k6\nor equivalent)

correctness --> testengines : shell out\n(external process)

store --> llm : scenario / instance\ngeneration (agreement Step 2)

note bottom of frontend
  **Implemented today**: a working prototype
  with all data mocked in-memory (see
  frontend/src/lib/mock/) -- no real backend,
  engine or storage exists yet.
end note

note bottom of k6adapter
  Only the k6 adapter is being built within
  the funded period. Additional EngineAdapter
  implementations (e.g. autocannon) are
  future work, not scheduled -- ADR 0001.
end note

legend right
  |     | Status |
  |<#d4edda>| Implemented |
  |<#fff3cd>| Proposed, not yet built |
  |<#e2e3e5>| External tool / third-party system |
endlegend

@enduml
